  "id": "principle-of-constancy",
  "term": "principle of constancy",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, the principle of constancy refers to the mind’s ability to think of the same thing across different moments and to recognize that it is doing so. It describes a psychological sense of sameness in meaning, whether or not the outside world itself is truly unchanged.",
